%% The control loop as a state machine.
%% The point of this diagram: verification is a CHECK, not a transition you
%% walk through. That is the bug lesson 03 naive.py demonstrates.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PENDING : goal accepted

    PENDING --> RUNNING : budget checked
    RUNNING --> RUNNING : action proposed, policy allowed, observation recorded

    RUNNING --> WAITING_APPROVAL : policy requires approval and none granted
    RUNNING --> COMPLETED : terminal action AND verification passed
    RUNNING --> FAILED : terminal action AND verification failed
    RUNNING --> BUDGET_EXHAUSTED : step, tool-call, retry, stall, time or cost limit hit
    RUNNING --> FAILED : tool retries exhausted for this action

    WAITING_APPROVAL --> RUNNING : a human approves, run resumes
    WAITING_APPROVAL --> FAILED : approval refused

    COMPLETED --> [*]
    FAILED --> [*]
    BUDGET_EXHAUSTED --> [*]

    note right of RUNNING
        One step = one decide + at most one act.
        A terminal decision costs exactly one step.
    end note

    note right of BUDGET_EXHAUSTED
        Every exit carries a labelled reason.
        There is no silent return.
    end note